  "slug": "simulations-structural-6310",
  "summary": "New work checks AlphaFold outputs against bilayer geometry and beta-sheet organization, while GPU frustration analysis scales to whole proteomes.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is assessing predicted structures with physically grounded criteria rather than a single static fold. AlphaFold-Multimer transmembrane complexes (~189k in the AFDB) are screened for bilayer compatibility, and AlphaFold3 pseudo-ensembles are tested on parallel versus antiparallel beta-sheet organization and polymorphism in short amyloidogenic peptides. The PyTorch Frustratometer reimplements local energetic frustration analysis with 70-13,000x GPU speedups and near-identical results, making proteome-scale analysis feasible. Related items extend sequence-level analysis: Omega-loop Gly/Pro flexibility and interface-dependent conservation, amino acid clustering and epistasis, and ContextMirror2.0 coevolutionary interactome prediction. These share an orientation toward evaluating models against physical or evolutionary constraints, not a single method. The previous MD-based items (BILBY, Cadense, bAIes) are not among the current items.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-13"
}
